# Email Broadcast Module Rules

This module adds marketing/broadcast email to EventFlow, kept architecturally
separate from transactional email (different code path, different compliance
rules, must never share a sending queue or fail together with transactional
sends).

## Non-negotiable architecture decisions
1. Our Postgres/Prisma DB is the source of truth for CONTACTS. Resend is the
   source of truth for per-email delivery/engagement events and the live
   unsubscribe action, but unsubscribe status is mirrored back into our DB via
   webhook so segment queries never depend on a live call to Resend.
2. Every contact gets an `isSubscribed` boolean (default true only when
   marketing consent was actually recorded — never default silently), plus
   `unsubscribedAt` and `unsubscribeSource`.
3. Before ANY broadcast send, filter the resolved segment locally by
   `isSubscribed = true` in Prisma. Never trust Resend alone to suppress
   recipients.
4. Every broadcast email must include Resend's `{{{RESEND_UNSUBSCRIBE_URL}}}`
   merge tag, enforced at template-render time — not left to user discretion.
   Refuse to send (return `{ success: false, error }`) if it's missing from
   compiled HTML.
5. Template editor: use Maily (`@maily-to/core`, `@maily-to/render`), the free
   MIT-licensed React/Tiptap email editor. Do not integrate Unlayer or any
   paid SDK without being asked.
6. Sending goes through Resend's Broadcast API (`resend.broadcasts.create`
   with `segmentId`), not raw `batch.send` loops, once a segment exceeds a
   small threshold.
7. All mutations (campaign create/update/send, template save, contact
   consent changes) are server actions per the general EventFlow rules —
   return `{ success, data?, error? }`. The one exception is the Resend
   webhook receiver, which must be a route handler
   (`src/app/api/webhooks/resend/route.ts`) since it's called by Resend, not
   by our own client.
8. Respect existing roles: MARKETING can create/send campaigns and view all
   guest data; SALES_REP should not get campaign-send access unless
   explicitly asked to extend that; ADMIN has full access.

## Data model additions (Prisma)
Add `EmailContact`, `EmailTemplate`, `EmailCampaign`,
`EmailCampaignRecipient`, `EmailEvent` models, following the naming/casing
conventions already used in schema.prisma. `EmailContact.guestId` is a
required relation to the existing `Guest` model — do not duplicate guest data
into this table beyond what's needed for send/consent state.

## Webhook safety
The Resend webhook route must verify signatures before processing, log every
raw event to `EmailEvent` first, then dispatch updates. Never trust an
unverified payload to flip `isSubscribed`.

## When in doubt
If a decision here conflicts with something faster/simpler, ask before
deviating — these constraints exist for compliance and data-integrity
reasons, not style preference.
